Fixed. The bug was in `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift:5` — the old implementation split the text on spaces and only kept tokens that *start* with `#`. That misses any tag that isn't a standalone space-delimited word, e.g. `list,#urgent.` (comma-attached) or `(#ideas)` (parenthesized).

The fix uses a regex `#([A-Za-z0-9_]+)` that scans the whole string for `#` followed by tag characters, returning matches in order of appearance.

Verified against a compiled harness (the sandbox blocks `swift test` in this environment):
- `hello #world #swift` → `["world","swift"]` ✓ (existing)
- `just plain text` → `[]` ✓ (existing)
- `shopping list,#urgent.` → `["urgent"]` ✓ (new)
- `(#ideas)` → `["ideas"]` ✓ (new)
- ordering across multiple tags preserved ✓

No existing behavior regressed. Temp harness removed.


